  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Sendai Framework Implementation investment, Geoscience Australia configured software used in Fiji&apos;s national earthquake monitoring and alerts centre, and provided training in real-time earthquake analysis to eight of the centre&apos;s staff, half of whom were women. Technical experts configured the so-called SeisComP software to ensure it appropriately detects earthquakes, including those that may generate a tsunami. And the training, delivered over a total of four weeks virtually and in country, helped build the technical competence and confidence of participants to undertake time-critical earthquake monitoring and analysis, including in generating tsunami warnings. Participants provided written feedback praising the training, with one participant saying it &apos;will 100 per cent help me in my work&apos;. With this training, it is hoped that the population of Fiji will receive more accurate and timely tsunami warnings, improving their hazard and disaster awareness, and lessening the impacts of future earthquakes and tsunamis.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
